# Warehouse camera recording (PrepCorex)

When the user asks about the **camera feature**, use this implementation as the current v1 baseline.

## Goal

Receiving start → operator phone records + client watches **live** → receive stop → local phone clip → confirmed upload to **admin Google Drive**.

## Agreed architecture

- **Camera:** phone/tablet browser camera on the warehouse receiving page
- **Recording:** MediaRecorder; pause/resume/stop; multiple clips per inbound request
- **Local storage:** completed Blob in IndexedDB on the same phone/browser until upload/removal
- **Live:** the same camera track publishes to managed LiveKit Cloud with short-lived server-issued tokens
- **Privacy:** client tokens work only for sessions whose `clientUserId` matches the signed-in user
- **Cloud storage:** resumable direct browser upload to private admin Google Drive; no video bytes in Vercel or Firebase
- **Metadata:** server-only `warehouseCameraSessions` collection stores lifecycle, request links, and Drive metadata
- **Live relay:** Managed LiveKit Cloud + short-lived PrepCorex viewer tokens (not raw RTSP to browser)

## Do not confuse with

- Existing barcode **scan camera** UI (`scan-camera-button`, etc.) — not video recording
- Receive **still photos** (Firebase Storage `warehouse-receive/…`)

## Spec / hooks

- Draft doc: `docs/WAREHOUSE_CAMERA_RECORDING.md` (update when implementing)
- Recorder: `warehouse-mobile-camera-recorder.tsx`
- Client viewer: Inventory live banner + per-inbound receive video dialog
- APIs: `src/app/api/warehouse-camera/`

